{% comment %}Guide text and category checks restored from the original standalone HTML.{% endcomment %}
<dialog id="ff-guide-basics" class="info-dialog" data-ff-guide-dialog aria-labelledby="ff-guide-basics-title"><button type="button" class="dialog-close icon-button" data-guide-close aria-label="Close information"><svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-close"/></svg></button><p class="eyebrow">THE REPLACEMENT CHECKLIST</p><h2 id="ff-guide-basics-title">Replacement part checklist.</h2><p>Begin with your existing part. A similar appearance is helpful, but it is only the first step.</p><h3>1. Compare the whole part</h3><p>Look at the front, back and side. Note the button or saddle shape, housing, mounting plate and the way the part attaches.</p><h3>2. Compare the measurements</h3><p>Match each label in the product drawing to the same location on your existing part. Keep hole diameter, post diameter and overall width separate.</p><h3>3. Check what connects to it</h3><p>Thread pitch, screw or pin positions, wiring and available clearance can matter as much as the outer dimensions. Check those details before choosing.</p><p>Style descriptions help you recognize a design. They do not establish interchangeability.</p></dialog>
<dialog id="ff-guide-measure" class="info-dialog" data-ff-guide-dialog aria-labelledby="ff-guide-measure-title"><button type="button" class="dialog-close icon-button" data-guide-close aria-label="Close information"><svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-close"/></svg></button><p class="eyebrow">FIT &amp; MEASURE</p><h2 id="ff-guide-measure-title">Measuring replacement parts.</h2><p>A number is only useful when you know where it starts and ends. Compare the same measurement on both parts, using the same units.</p><h3>Tuning machines</h3><p>Check the headstock hole, bushing, post height and mounting footprint separately. Use a rear view to compare screws or locating pins and the tuner orientation.</p><h3>Bridges and tailpieces</h3><p>Distinguish mounting-hole centres from string spacing. E-to-E means the distance between the two outside strings; adjacent-string spacing is a different measurement. Also check height, footprint and available cavity depth.</p><h3>Knobs and electronic parts</h3><p>Check the shaft diameter, shaft shape and fastening method. For pots and switches, also compare electrical specifications, terminals and cavity clearance.</p><p>Use measured product drawings for the exact variant you intend to buy. The sample drawings in this storefront preview are illustrative.</p></dialog>
<dialog id="ff-guide-finish" class="info-dialog" data-ff-guide-dialog aria-labelledby="ff-guide-finish-title"><button type="button" class="dialog-close icon-button" data-guide-close aria-label="Close information"><svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-close"/></svg></button><p class="eyebrow">FINISH GUIDE</p><h2 id="ff-guide-finish-title">Comparing hardware finishes.</h2><p>Compare the hardware you are keeping with the finish you are choosing. Look at the whole instrument in neutral daylight.</p><h3>Colour and surface are separate details</h3><p>Chrome, nickel, black and gold describe different finish families. Polished, satin and aged describe the surface appearance. Check both.</p><h3>Photographs are a reference</h3><p>Lighting, screen settings and wear can change how a finish appears. A new polished part can look different beside hardware that has aged through years of playing.</p><h3>Finish does not determine fit</h3><p>After choosing a look, check the dimensions and mounting details for that exact product variant.</p></dialog>
{% liquid
  capture ff_tuners
    render 'ff-category-url', collection: collections['tuners'], product_type: 'Guitar tuners', additional_types: 'Bass tuners|Classical tuners'
  endcapture
  capture ff_bridges
    render 'ff-category-url', collection: collections['bridges'], product_type: 'Tremolo bridges', additional_types: 'Bridge|Bridges|Fixed bridges|Tailpieces|Vibrato tailpieces'
  endcapture
  capture ff_pickups
    render 'ff-category-url', collection: collections['pickups'], product_type: 'Pickups'
  endcapture
  capture ff_electronics
    render 'ff-category-url', collection: collections['electronics'], product_type: 'Electronics'
  endcapture
  capture ff_pickguards
    render 'ff-category-url', collection: collections['pickguards'], product_type: 'Pickguards'
  endcapture
  capture ff_hardware
    render 'ff-category-url', collection: collections['hardware'], product_type: 'Saddles', additional_types: 'Knobs|Screws|Hardware'
  endcapture
%}
<dialog id="finder-dialog" class="finder-dialog" data-ff-guide-dialog aria-labelledby="ff-finder-overview-title"><button type="button" class="dialog-close icon-button" data-guide-close aria-label="Close information"><svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-close"/></svg></button><div id="finder-content">
<div data-ff-finder-panel=""><p class="eyebrow">PART SELECTION GUIDE</p><h2 id="ff-finder-overview-title" tabindex="-1">What are you replacing?</h2><p class="finder-lead">Select a part category to see which shapes, dimensions and installation details to compare with your existing part.</p><div class="finder-category-grid">
<button type="button" data-finder-category="tuners">{% render 'ff-atlas-image', index: 0, label: 'Tuners' %}<span>Tuners ↗</span></button>
<button type="button" data-finder-category="bridges">{% render 'ff-atlas-image', index: 1, label: 'Bridges & tailpieces' %}<span>Bridges &amp; tailpieces ↗</span></button>
<button type="button" data-finder-category="pickups">{% render 'ff-atlas-image', index: 2, label: 'Pickups' %}<span>Pickups ↗</span></button>
<button type="button" data-finder-category="electronics">{% render 'ff-atlas-image', index: 3, label: 'Electronics' %}<span>Electronics ↗</span></button>
<button type="button" data-finder-category="pickguards">{% render 'ff-atlas-image', index: 4, label: 'Pickguards & covers' %}<span>Pickguards &amp; covers ↗</span></button>
<button type="button" data-finder-category="small">{% render 'ff-atlas-image', index: 8, label: 'Hardware & small parts' %}<span>Hardware &amp; small parts ↗</span></button>
</div><p class="sample-note">This guide helps you compare parts. It does not identify or guarantee instrument compatibility.</p></div>
<div data-ff-finder-panel="tuners" hidden><p class="eyebrow">PART SELECTION GUIDE</p><h2 id="ff-finder-tuners-title" tabindex="-1">Choosing tuners.</h2><p class="finder-lead">Use your existing part as your reference. Compare the shape, mounting structure and all relevant measurements.</p><div class="finder-steps">
<div class="finder-step"><span>01</span><h3>Shape &amp; construction</h3><p>Compare the button shape and housing footprint.</p></div>
<div class="finder-step"><span>02</span><h3>Dimensions &amp; mounting</h3><p>Measure the headstock hole and bushing diameter separately.</p></div>
<div class="finder-step"><span>03</span><h3>Installation checks</h3><p>Check mounting screw or pin positions, post height and orientation.</p></div>
</div><div class="finder-checklist">Check the dimensions and installation details for the exact variant. Similar shapes and style names do not establish interchangeability.</div><div class="finder-bottom"><button type="button" class="text-link" data-finder>← All categories</button><a class="button dark" href="{{ ff_tuners | escape }}">Browse tuners <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a></div></div>
<div data-ff-finder-panel="bridges" hidden><p class="eyebrow">PART SELECTION GUIDE</p><h2 id="ff-finder-bridges-title" tabindex="-1">Choosing bridges &amp; tailpieces.</h2><p class="finder-lead">Use your existing part as your reference. Compare the shape, mounting structure and all relevant measurements.</p><div class="finder-steps">
<div class="finder-step"><span>01</span><h3>Shape &amp; construction</h3><p>Compare the mounting structure: screws, posts or hinge.</p></div>
<div class="finder-step"><span>02</span><h3>Dimensions &amp; mounting</h3><p>Measure mounting centres and string spacing separately.</p></div>
<div class="finder-step"><span>03</span><h3>Installation checks</h3><p>Check the footprint, available height and cavity depth.</p></div>
</div><div class="finder-checklist">Check the dimensions and installation details for the exact variant. Similar shapes and style names do not establish interchangeability.</div><div class="finder-bottom"><button type="button" class="text-link" data-finder>← All categories</button><a class="button dark" href="{{ ff_bridges | escape }}">Browse bridges &amp; tailpieces <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a></div></div>
<div data-ff-finder-panel="pickups" hidden><p class="eyebrow">PART SELECTION GUIDE</p><h2 id="ff-finder-pickups-title" tabindex="-1">Choosing pickups.</h2><p class="finder-lead">Use your existing part as your reference. Compare the shape, mounting structure and all relevant measurements.</p><div class="finder-steps">
<div class="finder-step"><span>01</span><h3>Shape &amp; construction</h3><p>Compare the pickup footprint, mounting ears and cover.</p></div>
<div class="finder-step"><span>02</span><h3>Dimensions &amp; mounting</h3><p>Measure pole spacing, mounting centres and cavity depth.</p></div>
<div class="finder-step"><span>03</span><h3>Installation checks</h3><p>Check pickup position, wiring and electrical specifications.</p></div>
</div><div class="finder-checklist">Check the dimensions and installation details for the exact variant. Similar shapes and style names do not establish interchangeability.</div><div class="finder-bottom"><button type="button" class="text-link" data-finder>← All categories</button><a class="button dark" href="{{ ff_pickups | escape }}">Browse pickups <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a></div></div>
<div data-ff-finder-panel="electronics" hidden><p class="eyebrow">PART SELECTION GUIDE</p><h2 id="ff-finder-electronics-title" tabindex="-1">Choosing electronics.</h2><p class="finder-lead">Use your existing part as your reference. Compare the shape, mounting structure and all relevant measurements.</p><div class="finder-steps">
<div class="finder-step"><span>01</span><h3>Shape &amp; construction</h3><p>Identify the component type, terminals and shaft shape.</p></div>
<div class="finder-step"><span>02</span><h3>Dimensions &amp; mounting</h3><p>Measure shaft diameter, threaded length and mounting clearance.</p></div>
<div class="finder-step"><span>03</span><h3>Installation checks</h3><p>Check resistance, taper, circuit type and wiring before selecting.</p></div>
</div><div class="finder-checklist">Check the dimensions and installation details for the exact variant. Similar shapes and style names do not establish interchangeability.</div><div class="finder-bottom"><button type="button" class="text-link" data-finder>← All categories</button><a class="button dark" href="{{ ff_electronics | escape }}">Browse electronics <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a></div></div>
<div data-ff-finder-panel="pickguards" hidden><p class="eyebrow">PART SELECTION GUIDE</p><h2 id="ff-finder-pickguards-title" tabindex="-1">Choosing pickguards &amp; covers.</h2><p class="finder-lead">Use your existing part as your reference. Compare the shape, mounting structure and all relevant measurements.</p><div class="finder-steps">
<div class="finder-step"><span>01</span><h3>Shape &amp; construction</h3><p>Compare the full outline and pickup cutouts.</p></div>
<div class="finder-step"><span>02</span><h3>Dimensions &amp; mounting</h3><p>Compare every screw position; hole count alone is not enough.</p></div>
<div class="finder-step"><span>03</span><h3>Installation checks</h3><p>Check thickness, neck cutout and bridge clearance.</p></div>
</div><div class="finder-checklist">Check the dimensions and installation details for the exact variant. Similar shapes and style names do not establish interchangeability.</div><div class="finder-bottom"><button type="button" class="text-link" data-finder>← All categories</button><a class="button dark" href="{{ ff_pickguards | escape }}">Browse pickguards &amp; covers <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a></div></div>
<div data-ff-finder-panel="small" hidden><p class="eyebrow">PART SELECTION GUIDE</p><h2 id="ff-finder-small-title" tabindex="-1">Choosing hardware &amp; small parts.</h2><p class="finder-lead">Use your existing part as your reference. Compare the shape, mounting structure and all relevant measurements.</p><div class="finder-steps">
<div class="finder-step"><span>01</span><h3>Shape &amp; construction</h3><p>Compare the shape, mounting method and included pieces.</p></div>
<div class="finder-step"><span>02</span><h3>Dimensions &amp; mounting</h3><p>Check hole sizes, thread pitch and mating surfaces.</p></div>
<div class="finder-step"><span>03</span><h3>Installation checks</h3><p>Compare all dimensions, not just the overall appearance.</p></div>
</div><div class="finder-checklist">Check the dimensions and installation details for the exact variant. Similar shapes and style names do not establish interchangeability.</div><div class="finder-bottom"><button type="button" class="text-link" data-finder>← All categories</button><a class="button dark" href="{{ ff_hardware | escape }}">Browse hardware &amp; small parts <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a></div></div>
</div></dialog>
